From: canoziia <canoziia@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] deepseek-v4-flash: small-M dense FP8 decode GEMMs

VLLM_DSV4_DENSE_FP8_DECODE (default 0). DeepSeek-V4-Flash dense projections
are FP8 e4m3 with 128x128 e8m0 block scales and run through Marlin FP8
(group 128) on sm_80. The DeepSeek V4.1 dense MXFP8 decode kernels
(deepseek-v4.1-flash 0013, _dsv41_dense_mxfp8.so) read the same Marlin 8-bit
weight layout with e8m0 group-32 scales; a block scale is the same value for
each of its group-32 slots, so at load the block scales are expanded into a
group-32 copy (N*K/32 bytes, ~3 % of the weight; ~60 MiB per PP3 rank).
Dequantised weights are bit-identical to Marlin's; only the fp32
accumulation order differs (fixed order, deterministic, graph safe).

Per (K, N) and M tier a cold-L2 scan on CMP 170HX picked stream-K (M <= 8)
or split-K (M <= 64) configurations; a tier is used only where it beat
Marlin by >= 3 %. Other shapes, M > 64, bias or scales that are not powers of
two in [2^-126, 2^7] keep Marlin. One layer's six dense projections:
M=1 126 -> 107 us, M=4 118 -> 105, M=24 142 -> 120, M=32 140 -> 133,
M=64 223 -> 186 us. models/deepseek-v4-flash/tests/test_dense_fp8_decode_gpu.py.
